        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An electric snow shovel is the right tool for steps, decks, walkways and short driveways in light, dry snow. It is light, quick to start, easy to store and spares you from lifting, which is exactly what most people want for the small, awkward areas around a house.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            It is the wrong tool for a big driveway, heavy wet snow, deep overnight storms, gravel or the plow berm. If those describe your winters, put the money into a proper machine from our electric snow blower rankings first, and add a power shovel later for the jobs a blower cannot reach.
          </p>
